      "text": [
        " قُلْتُ لِأَبِي عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) أَدْنَى مَا يَقْصُرُ فِيهِ الْمُسَافِرُ فَقَالَ بَرِيدٌ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "And from him, from his father, from Ibn Abu Umeyr, from Abu Ayoub who said, ",
          "‘I said to Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup>, ‘The least of what the traveler would be shortening (his <span class=\"iTxt\">Salāt</span>) in?’ So he<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘A <span class=\"iTxt\">Bareyd</span> (12 miles approx.)’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "2. It is a narration from him (narrator of previous Hadith) by his father from ibn abu ‘Umayr from abu Ayyub who has said the following: “I once asked abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, about the minimum distance after the traveling of which a traveler reduces his Salah (prayer). He (the Imam) said, ‘It is one barid.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
